      <div type="clause" n="El. 49.2">
        <head><ref type="lawCode" target="law:Af">Af</ref> El. 49.2</head>
        <ab type="liebermannText" xml:lang="ang" source="#liebermann" n="El. 49.2" corresp="#wit-e"><pb n="42" ed="#liebermann"/>Þa hie<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="22" target="#Af_El-to-49-2.lnote.oe.22"/> ða ongeaton<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="31" target="#Af_El-to-49-2.lnote.oe.31"/>, þæt him ne<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="*" target="#Af_El-to-49-2.lnote.oe.star"/> speow<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="32" target="#Af_El-to-49-2.lnote.oe.32"/>, ða sendon hie<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="22" target="#Af_El-to-49-2.lnote.oe.22"/> ærendgewrit to him. Þis is ðonne þæt<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="33" target="#Af_El-to-49-2.lnote.oe.33"/> ærendgewrit þe ða apostolas sendon ealle to Antiohhia<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="29" target="#Af_El-to-49-2.lnote.oe.29"/> ⁊ to<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="33" target="#Af_El-to-49-2.lnote.oe.33"/> Syria ⁊ to Cilicia, ða sint<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="34" target="#Af_El-to-49-2.lnote.oe.34"/> nu of hæðenum<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="35" target="#Af_El-to-49-2.lnote.oe.35"/> ðeodu<hi rend="italic">m</hi> to Criste<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="36" target="#Af_El-to-49-2.lnote.oe.36"/> gecirde:</ab>
        <ab type="liebermannText" xml:lang="ang" source="#liebermann" n="El. 49.2" corresp="#wit-g-prol-only"><pb n="42" ed="#liebermann"/>Þa hí ða ongeaton, þ<hi rend="italic">æt</hi> hi<hi rend="italic">m</hi> ne speow, ða sendon hí ærendgewrit tó hím. Ðis ys þ<hi rend="italic">æt</hi> ærendgewrit ðe ða apostolas sendon ealle tó Antiochia ⁊ Siria ⁊ to Cilicia, ða sint nú of æðenum ðeodum tó Criste gecyrred:</ab>
        <ab type="liebermannText" xml:lang="ang" source="#liebermann" n="El. 49.2" corresp="#wit-h"><pb n="43" ed="#liebermann"/>Ða hy ongeaton<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="16" target="#Af_El-to-49-2.lnote.oe.16"/>, ðæt him ne speow, ða sendon hy<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="7" target="#Af_El-to-49-2.lnote.oe.7"/> [æ]rendgewrit<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="17" target="#Af_El-to-49-2.lnote.oe.17"/> to him. [Ð]is is ðonne þæt ærendgewritt<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="18" target="#Af_El-to-49-2.lnote.oe.18"/> ðe þa apostolas sendon<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="2" target="#Af_El-to-49-2.lnote.oe.2"/> ealle to Antiochia ond<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="2" target="#Af_El-to-49-2.lnote.oe.2"/> to Syria ond<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="2" target="#Af_El-to-49-2.lnote.oe.2"/> to Cilitia, ða sind nu of hæðnum<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="14" target="#Af_El-to-49-2.lnote.oe.14"/> ðeodum to Cryste gecyrrede:<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="19" target="#Af_El-to-49-2.lnote.oe.19"/></ab>
        <ab type="liebermannText" xml:lang="la" source="#liebermann" n="El. 49.2" corresp="#wit-q"><pb n="43" ed="#liebermann"/>Et cum cognouissent, quid inter eos ageretur, scripserunt eis. Et hęc est epistola, quam apostoli miserunt omnibus Antiochiam, Syriam<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="17" target="#Af_El-to-49-2.lnote.oe.17-2"/> et Ciliciam<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="15" target="#Af_El-to-49-2.lnote.oe.15"/>, qui nunc ex gentili seruitute conuersi sunt ad Dominum:</ab>
        <ab type="editionText" xml:lang="ang" source="#jurasinski-and-oliver" n="Mp 49.2" corresp="#wit-e"><pb n="266" ed="#jurasinski-and-oliver"/>Þa hie ða ongeaton, þæt him ne speow, ða sendon hie ærendgewrit to him. Þis is ðonne þæt ærendgewrit þe ða apostolas sendon ealle to Antiohhia ⁊ to Syria ⁊ to Cilicia, ða sint nu of hæðenum ðeodu<hi rend="italic">m</hi> to Criste gecirde:</ab>
        <ab type="translation" xml:lang="de" source="#liebermann"><pb n="43" ed="#liebermann"/>Als sie nun erfuhren, dass [es<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="1" target="#Af_El-to-49-2.lnote.de.1"/>] jenen nicht glückte, da sandten sie ein Sendschreiben an sie.<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="2" target="#Af_El-to-49-2.lnote.de.2"/> Dies [folgende] ist nun das Sendschreiben, welches die Apostel alle sandten nach Antiochia und nach Syrien und nach Cilicien, welche [Länder] jetzt<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="3" target="#Af_El-to-49-2.lnote.de.3"/> von heidnischen<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="4" target="#Af_El-to-49-2.lnote.de.4"/> Völkern<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="5" target="#Af_El-to-49-2.lnote.de.5"/> zu Christo bekehrt sind:</ab>
        <ab type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude" ana="#fromGerman">When they then learned that [it] was not succeeding for those [messengers], they sent a letter to them. This [following] is the letter which the apostles all sent to Antioch and to Syria and to Cilicia, which [lands] are now converted from heathen peoples to Christ:</ab>
        <ab type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#jurasinski-and-oliver" corresp="#wit-e"><pb n="267" ed="#jurasinski-and-oliver"/>When they perceived that they had no success, then they sent a written message to them. This is the document that the apostles sent together to Antioch and to Syria and to Cilicia, which were then newly turned from heathen observances to Christ:</ab>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="Af_El-to-49-2.lnote.oe.22" n="22" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">42</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">hi <hi rend="italic">Ld</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">hi Ld</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="Af_El-to-49-2.lnote.oe.31" n="31" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">42</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">-gioton <hi rend="italic">So;</hi> -gyaton <hi rend="italic">Ld</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">-gioton So; -gyaton Ld</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="Af_El-to-49-2.lnote.oe.star" n="*" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">42</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">belampe <hi rend="italic">statt</hi> ne speow <hi rend="italic">Ld.; vgl. Quadr.</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">belampe instead of ne speow Ld.; cf. Quadr.</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="Af_El-to-49-2.lnote.oe.32" n="32" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">42</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">-we <hi rend="italic">So</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">-we So</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="Af_El-to-49-2.lnote.oe.33" n="33" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">42</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de"><hi rend="italic">fehlt Ld</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">lacking in Ld</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="Af_El-to-49-2.lnote.oe.29" n="29" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">42</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">-ochia <hi rend="italic">So Ld</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">-ochia So Ld</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="Af_El-to-49-2.lnote.oe.34" n="34" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">42</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">sind <hi rend="italic">Ld</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">sind Ld</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="Af_El-to-49-2.lnote.oe.35" n="35" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">42</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">-nu <hi rend="italic">So</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">-nu So</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="Af_El-to-49-2.lnote.oe.36" n="36" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">42</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">Crist gecyrd <hi rend="italic">So Ld</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">Crist gecyrd So Ld</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="Af_El-to-49-2.lnote.oe.16" n="16" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">43</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">a <hi rend="italic">übergeschr.</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">a written above</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="Af_El-to-49-2.lnote.oe.7" n="7" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">43</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">y <hi rend="italic">auf Rasur</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">y on an erasure</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="Af_El-to-49-2.lnote.oe.17" n="17" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">43</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">rendgewrit to h. is is ð. þ. <hi rend="italic">am Rande nachgetragen</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">rendgewrit to h. is is ð. þ. added later in the margin</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="Af_El-to-49-2.lnote.oe.18" n="18" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">43</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de"><hi rend="italic">letztes</hi> t <hi rend="italic">geänd. aus</hi> e</seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">last t altered from e</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="Af_El-to-49-2.lnote.oe.2" n="2" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">43</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">o <hi rend="italic">geänd. in</hi> a</seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">o altered to a</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="Af_El-to-49-2.lnote.oe.14" n="14" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">43</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de"><hi rend="italic">geänd. in</hi> hæðen.</seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">altered to hæðen.</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="Af_El-to-49-2.lnote.oe.19" n="19" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">43</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">gec <hi rend="italic">am Rande, Rest auf Rasur</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">gec in the margin, the rest on an erasure</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="Af_El-to-49-2.lnote.oe.17-2" n="17" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">43</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">Sir. <hi rend="italic">R</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">Sir. R</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="Af_El-to-49-2.lnote.oe.15" n="15" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">43</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">Cyl. <hi rend="italic">Dm</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">Cyl. Dm</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="erklaerung" xml:id="Af_El-to-49-2.lnote.de.1" n="1" source="#liebermann-erkl"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">3</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">48</biblScope><biblScope unit="column">1</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">‘Bei ihnen keinen guten Fortgang habe’ Schmid. Ælfred meint, den Missionaren gelang das Bekehren nicht, durch die störende judenchristliche <hi rend="italic">facta seditio Paulo; A. ap.</hi> 15, 2. Kirchlicher vertuschend setzte dafür ein neutrales ‘Geschehen’ ein Schreider, dem Ld Q folgen. Irrig meint Koerner (<hi rend="italic">s. u.</hi> 49, 4), Q verstehe Af nicht, und Turk, Lambarde übersetze aus Br ins Agsä. zurück</seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">‘were not making good progress among them’ Schmid. Ælfred means that the missionaries did not succeed in converting people, owing to the disruptive Judaeo-Christian <hi rend="italic">facta seditio Paulo; A. ap.</hi> 15, 2. In a more ecclesiastical spirit of glossing over this, a scribe substituted a neutral ‘happening’, which Ld Q follow. Koerner (<hi rend="italic">see below</hi> 49, 4) wrongly thinks that Q does not understand Af, and Turk that Lambarde translates back from Br into Anglo-Saxon</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="erklaerung" xml:id="Af_El-to-49-2.lnote.de.2" n="2" source="#liebermann-erkl"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">3</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">48</biblScope><biblScope unit="column">1</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">Syrer</seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">Syrians</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="erklaerung" xml:id="Af_El-to-49-2.lnote.de.3" n="3" source="#liebermann-erkl"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">3</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">48</biblScope><biblScope unit="column">1</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">Af meint nicht das 9. Jh., sondern nimmt aus Vulg. den Zwischensatz der Adresse des folgenden Briefes</seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">Af does not mean the 9th cent., but takes from the Vulg. the parenthetical clause of the address of the following letter</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="erklaerung" xml:id="Af_El-to-49-2.lnote.de.4" n="4" source="#liebermann-erkl"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">3</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">48</biblScope><biblScope unit="column">1</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">G zeigt Abfall des anlautenden <hi rend="italic">h-</hi>; <hi rend="italic">s. d. Wb</hi> 2a</seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">G shows loss of initial <hi rend="italic">h-</hi>; <hi rend="italic">see</hi> that word in <hi rend="italic">Wb</hi> 2a</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="erklaerung" xml:id="Af_El-to-49-2.lnote.de.5" n="5" source="#liebermann-erkl"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">3</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">48</biblScope><biblScope unit="column">1</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">Q meinte wohl <hi rend="italic">ðeowdome</hi> zu lesen</seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">Q probably thought he was reading <hi rend="italic">ðeowdome</hi></seg></note>
      </div>
